# ---- CREDENTIALS ----------------------------------------------------
# This repo is public. Everything here is a file that has, in real
# projects, been committed by someone running `git add -A` in a hurry.

# The Firebase admin key. `serviceAccount.json` is the name our scripts
# default to — but the file the Firebase console actually hands you is
# called pickem-c0d06-firebase-adminsdk-XXXXX-YYYYYYYY.json, and THAT
# name was not covered. check.sh only ever looked for the tidy name too,
# so it printed "service account not in git" with the real key staged.
serviceAccount.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*-service-account*.json

# Wrangler's local secrets file. worker/wrangler.toml names three secrets
# set with `wrangler secret put`: SA_JSON (the whole admin key),
# RESEND_KEY, and ADMIN_KEY (which guards endpoints that send real
# notifications to real phones). .dev.vars is where all three end up the
# first time anyone runs the Worker locally.
.dev.vars
worker/.dev.vars
.env
.env.*

*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# ---- TOOL STATE -----------------------------------------------------
.wrangler/
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
*firebase-debug*.log
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The test suite runs against a Playwright install that is not part of
# this repo (see scripts/test/README.md). Nothing here is source.
# NOTE: no trailing slash — a bare `node_modules/` does not match a
# SYMLINK named node_modules, which is how it is set up locally, so git
# offered to commit a broken link.
node_modules
scripts/test/screens/
